{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And these are the days of the years of the life of Abraham which he lived.</b> The verse is precise in saying ״which he lived״ — according to the words of the Sages, whose memory is for blessing (Genesis Rabbah 63), who said that five years were subtracted from him on account of the day on which Esau committed five transgressions. Therefore it says <b>which he lived</b> — meaning: not the years that were decreed for him, for they were more, but these are what he actually lived." "<b>Thus concludes the portion of חיי שרה</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:12.488930805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}